{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Disposition correction (orchestrator, 2026-08-30): NOT superseded — ready-to-fix, deferred behind eb64\n\nA prior orchestrator note tentatively framed this ticket as \"resolved/superseded by ce6b\" (branch-6 narrowing → `command_failed`). **That framing was wrong and is retracted.** Re-reading this ticket's own record:\n\n- The **operator already decided this ticket (2026-08-30, comment above)**: `ExpressionError` maps to a **new dedicated `expression_unresolved` code**, explicitly rejecting BOTH `llm_unavailable` (false outage) AND `command_failed` (too vague to guide retry-vs-fix on `run_workflow`), citing gRPC/HTTP status-code precedent. So `command_failed` is the very outcome the operator ruled out — ce6b does not resolve this ticket.\n- ce6b (`bleareyed-claimable-quelea`) is the **separate follow-up this ticket's own decision calls for** (\"narrow branch 6 to `LLMUnavailableError` … File discovered_from this ticket\"), and is linked `discovered_from` 73d8. The two **compose, not conflict**: 73d8 sets an explicit `error_code = \"expression_unresolved\"` on `ExpressionError` so `error_code_for` **branch 5** fires before branch 6; ce6b then narrows **branch 6** for every *other* non-outage `LLMError`. Neither supersedes the other.\n\n**Status: ready-to-fix (decision made), no remaining design question.** Blast radius is small: set the `error_code` attribute on `ExpressionError` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py:251`), add `expression_unresolved` to `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (`src/rebar/_errors.py`) + the taxonomy contract test, and add held-out tests through the real `run_workflow` surface (outage still `llm_unavailable`; `ExpressionError` → `expression_unresolved`). Origin `8a31` to be recorded `caused_by` at close.\n\n**Deferred behind epic eb64 (`financial-stoneware-brant`):** the fix site `src/rebar/llm/workflow/executor.py` is inside eb64's declared `src/rebar/llm/` scope (runner lifecycle / LLM config convergence). Launching a parallel agent now would edit files the epic is actively converging. Tagging `eb64-coord` and adding `depends_on eb64` so `ready`/`next-batch` hold it until the epic lands, then fix it (with ce6b) against the converged surface."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788130407946062039,"uuid":"d1455bb3-a8c0-4b73-95c6-926ce4099825"}